  "reason": "The existing evidence shows that configurations using pca_n2000 RNA encoder and imagenet_vit_l image encoder (e.g., config_030) achieve high accuracy (0.635). This experiment tests a similar setup with transformer aggregation (vs. avgpool in config_030) and weighted fusion, which could improve accuracy by leveraging more complex feature interactions. It balances exploration (testing a different aggregation method) and exploitation (building on the success of pca_n2000 RNA). The expected cost is moderate (likely ~6-7 GPU hours), allowing room for further experiments."
